{"agent":"lane-infra-bugs","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The diff threads `env_extra` from `_merged_range_env` through `_run_under_slot`/`_run_locked` into `_execute`, but the only shown change to `_execute` is its signature/docstring; the body is unchanged and therefore does not add `env_extra` to the child process environment. Given a post-merge run where `changed_from` is a known base, `_merged_range_env` returns the two `PRE_COMMIT_*` variables, `_execute` accepts them but drops them, and the hook command still inherits no `PRE_COMMIT_FROM_REF`. `scripts/ci/gitleaks-pushed.sh` then falls back to `origin/main..HEAD` and scans the large set of unpushed local commits, which is the original CI failure.","digest":"935031b0c658c647","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_execute","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_execute"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"This is the earlier “does not derive the merge’s first-parent range” defect, moved to the new helper: `_merged_range_env` only maps an already supplied `changed_from` and returns `{}` when it is empty. If the after-merge check is invoked without `changed_from` (the reported symptom is that no `PRE_COMMIT_FROM_REF` is exported) while the enclosing run already knows the merge `base`, the function still exports no range and `gitleaks-pushed.sh` again scans `origin/main..HEAD`. Even when `changed_from` is a moving ref such as `main`, it is resolved in `repo` before the suite-slot wait; if `main` advances from `A` to `B` while queued, `_run_under_slot` merges onto `B` to avoid a stale tree, but the hook receives `PRE_COMMIT_FROM_REF=A` and scans `A..HEAD`, including the `A..B` commits that were not part of this merge. The range should be derived/re-resolved from the actual merged tree’s first parent, and `PRE_COMMIT_TO_REF` should be the resolved merge commit rather than a late-bound `HEAD`.","digest":"6273512677c2d6b8","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_merged_range_env","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_merged_range_env"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The added regression test does not exercise the reported failure path. Both tests call `CI.run(..., changed_from=before)` (lines 51 and 69), so they only test the case where the caller already supplies the range. The bug is that the post-merge CI check runs without `PRE_COMMIT_FROM_REF` (per the lane note, without a usable `changed_from`), causing `gitleaks-pushed.sh` to fall back to `origin/main..HEAD`. A test that always passes `changed_from` will pass even if the fix only forwards an explicitly supplied range and still does not derive/export the merge's first-parent range for the after-merge hook. Add a test that invokes the after-merge check exactly as the post-merge hook does (no `changed_from`) and asserts the hook sees the merge range, or directly test the range-derivation helper for a merge commit.","digest":"d8a1a1f6d26c4645","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_ci_merge_range_env.py:51","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_ci_merge_range_env.py:51"}],"chunks_total":2,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":9766,"diff_sha":"e2ee0d2d8576bc455ee3f08c7ef39800046314bc6e64ac3f7dc0414c5268e023","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Bci-gitleaks-over-the-pushed-commi-858efc87b3-e32e69f","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":203.8,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"d8f22e8d755d5607","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bci-gitleaks-over-the-pushed-commi-858efc87b3-e32e69f.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261112T222818Z-294cec4f.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794522702.8740585,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"},{"at":1794522703.0539079,"family":"xai","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"grok-4.7","reason":"HTTP 403","reviewer":"grok-4.7"}],"review_id":"2d60980ba978","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"534562bf28ba99d3ec1effd2daad79ac928d6cc2","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py":"100644 af65d20741735dde76dbc0c876ddf3e3c5b42ad0","tests/test_ci_merge_range_env.py":"100644 e4001d8083ec2f3156514198e54bcce50c136582"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":2,"rounds":2,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_execute","ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_merged_range_env","tests/test_ci_merge_range_env.py:51"],"tree_sha":"534562bf28ba+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e0c5a17850fc5d3b0c50853aa","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":187490,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bci-gitleaks-over-the-pushed-commi-858efc87b3-e32e69f","ts":"2026-11-12T22:31:46.169515Z"}
